{"type": "thinking", "text": "Sell Old Gear sheet lists candidates: Adamantite Platebody, Agility Cape, Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger, Gilded Platebody, Iron Sword, Mercantile Cape, Mithril Med Helmet, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody. Interesting. Need to evaluate eligibility: \"outdated-equipment bulk action: its candidate set is now computed by a simplified eligibility filter.\"\n\nWeapons: equipped Iron Sword (Weapon (Atk)). Inventory has Iron Sword x3. Old gear action lists Iron Sword ×2 (keeping 1 equipped? or keep one?). Hmm. It includes equipped items? Let's think.\n\nCandidates expected for outdated equipment: items that are worse than equipped and sellable. But it's including many platebodies — Adamantite, Gilded, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody, Mithril Med Helmet, Agility Cape, Mercantile Cape, Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger.\n\nWait, armor slots: equipped only Bronze Boots (feet). So platebodies aren't equipped. The candidate set should perhaps be old gear = lower tier than best. But there's no equipped body armor, so platebodies might be considered \"outdated\" relative to...? Hmm.\n\nWait preconditions inventory: Mithril Platebody, Adamantite Platebody, Slayer Platebody, Runite Chainbody, Runite Platebody and Gilded Platebody each x1. But Sell Old Gear candidate list includes Adamantite, Gilded, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody but not Slayer Platebody or Runite Platebody. Hmm interesting. Why those? Maybe \"simplified eligibility filter\" bug: it's including items of value >= something while excluding higher ones? Or maybe the filter checks \"item is not best in slot\"? Slayer Platebody and Runite Platebody excluded because... maybe they're best? Let's check item stats.\n\nAlso Agility Cape and Mercantile Cape — capes. Bronze Axe and Bronze Dagger are weapons; equipped weapon is Iron Sword. Bronze Axe may be a tool though. Hmm.\n\nActually the Sell sheet says \"Sell Old Gear\". Let's see expected behavior. We need to determine if candidate set has clear bug. Potentially \"simplified eligibility filter\" could mistakenly include equipment better than currently equipped. For example Gilded Platebody might be better than nothing? With no body armor equipped, any platebody is an upgrade, so none should be \"old gear\". Hmm but that's ambiguous.\n\nLet me consider: maybe eligibility is defined as \"items that are not equipped and are of lower value than the highest-value item in that slot\". With no equipped body armor, nothing to compare... but lists four platebodies and helmet, capes. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively maybe \"simplified filter\" checks whether item's stat is less than the currently equipped item in its slot; for empty slots, everything qualifies. That might be intended? \"Outdated equipment\" sold when you have better. If no armor equipped, then all armor gets sold — that's dangerous but maybe intended simple.\n\nActually let's get more info. Cancel out and inspect individual item details? The shop sell list shows items. Maybe long press for details? Let me check what the quest log says and other data.\n\nBetter approach: understand the app's data through UI. Let me first test the toggle persistence, which is a clear change. Then the bulk actions, then quest log.\n\nToggle test: currently off. Turn on, go Home, reopen shop Sell, check state. Also maybe toggle on then leave shop via back and reopen.\n\nLet me cancel sheet first."}
