r unused materials based on crafting recipes → likely misclassifies items (sells useful materials, or excludes junk).\n\nLet's focus on finding concrete bugs.\n\nFor Sell Old Gear candidate set, let's reason: The candidate list: Adamantite Platebody, Agility Cape, Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger, Gilded Platebody, Iron Sword ×2, Mercantile Cape, Mithril Med Helmet, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody.\n\nInventory equipment available: Bronze Dagger, Iron Sword (equipped), Adamantite Platebody, Agility Cape, Bronze Boots (equipped), Gilded Platebody, Mercantile Cape, Mithril Med Helmet, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody, Runite Platebody, Slayer Platebody, Steel Full Helmet, Bronze Axe (equipped?), Bronze Fishing Rod (equipped), Bronze Pickaxe (equipped).\n\nExpected \"old gear\" perhaps = gear worse than currently equipped in the same slot, excluding equipped items and best-tier alternatives you might want. But no body/head/cape equipped. Yet the app lists many. Maybe the app considers equipment outdated if there's a better item owned. E.g., among platebodies: Runite Platebody is highest; Slayer Platebody lower; Mithril, Adamantite, Gilded lower. If filter computes best owned per slot, all lower tiers are outdated: Adamantite, Gilded, Mithril, Slayer, Runite Chainbody (chainbody vs platebody?), Steel Full Helmet (helmet), Mithril Med Helmet (helmet). But Runite Platebody (best) should be excluded. Slayer Platebody (probably low) should be included — but it's excluded! Why? Maybe because its sell price is 225 (lowest) and filter uses value threshold? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the filter is \"sell price > some threshold\" or \">= 300\"? candidates prices: Adamantite 937, Gilded 300, Mithril Platebody 625, Runite Chainbody 1250, Mercantile Cape 6, Agility Cape 6, Bronze Axe 25, Bronze Dagger 25, Iron Sword 62, Mithril Med Helmet 437. Excluded: Slayer Platebody (225), Runite Platebody (1250), Steel Full Helmet (218), plus equipped items. That doesn't fit price threshold (6 included, 225 excluded).\n\nMaybe filter is based on \"is this item's stats worse than an equipped or owned item of same slot\"? Let's check stats:\n- Runite Platebody vs Runite Chainbody: Platebody better defense. So chainbody outdated. Slayer Platebody maybe has special stats? Might be better than? Hmm.\n- Steel Full Helmet vs Mithril Med Helmet: Mithril Med better, so Steel Full Helmet should be outdated, but it's excluded! And Mithril Med Helmet included (maybe there is an even better helmet owned? No). Hmm contradictory.\n\nActually maybe I misread the list. Let me re-open Sell Old Gear and capture full list carefully, maybe scroll. But the sheet showed 10 items and total 5,428. Let me compute candidates prices: 937+6+25+25+300+124+6+437+625+1250 = 3,735? Wait that's not 5,428. Let's recalc: Adamantite 937, Agility 6, Bronze Axe 25, Bronze Dagger 25, Gilded 300, Iron Sword 124 (x2 at 62), Mercantile 6, Mithril Med 437, Mithril Plate 625, Runite Chain 1250. Sum = 937+6=943, +25=968, +25=993, +300=1293, +124=1417, +6=1423, +437=1860, +625=2485, +1250=3735. But total displayed 5,428. Discrepancy! Hmm maybe totals include other items not listed? Or prices in list might be different from sell prices? Let's re-check. In sell list, Iron Sword 62 ea with x3; old gear x2 = 124. Gilded 300. Total 5428 differs by 1693. Maybe the sheet has more items below Runite Chainbody that need scroll? The sheet list ended at Runite Chainbody at y=1949, total at 2031, and buttons at 2149. Maybe there are additional entries below requiring scroll within sheet? The sheet are visible; maybe scrollable. Hmm.\n\nWait maybe some listed prices are per-item values but multiplied by quantity other than 1. Bronze Axe in inventory x2 (one equipped?) — old gear list says Bronze Axe ×1. Iron Sword ×2. Others ×1. Total 3735. Not 5428. Could there be items hidden above Adamantite? The top of sheet starts at title y=1063, first item y=1165. So no.\n\nMaybe the total includes items not displayed because list is scrollable and cut? There's space between last item row (1949) and total (2031), so maybe not.\n\nLet's re-open sheet and scroll inside to see. But this discrepancy might be a mere display artifact of \"sell price\" vs \"value\". Let's check by tapping Sell All would change data massively; avoid. We can compare total after cancel. Hmm.\n\nActually the total might be sum of full \"value\" (some price different). Let me see: 5,428 - 3,735 = 1,693. Interesting numbers: Slayer Platebody 225 + Steel Full Helmet 218 + Runite Platebody 1250 = 1693! Yes! 225+218+1250 = 1693. So the total includes three items not displayed in the list: Slayer Platebody, Steel Full Helmet, Runite Platebody! That means the visible list might be clipped or... Wait those items are the ones I expected to be excluded. Interesting! The total includes them but they're not shown? Or they are shown but off-screen and my observation only captured some elements? Actually observe listed elements [0]-[36], total and buttons. If there were more rows, they'd appear. Unless the sheet is scrollable and rows above? Hmm.\n\nHold on: The total includes exactly the three excluded items' sell prices. That suggests the actual candidate set includes ALL unequipped armor/weapons: Adamantite, Agility, Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger, Gilded, Iron Sword x2, Mercantile, Mithril Med, Mithril Plate, Runite Chain, Runite Plate, Slayer, Steel Full. Sum = 3735+1693 = 5428. Yes! So the candidate set is all non-equipped items except... wait what about Bronze Pickaxe, Bronze Fishing Rod? Those are tools equipped (excluded). Bronze Boots equipped excluded. Bronze Axe \"(equipped)\" but x2 in inventory — list includes Bronze Axe ×1! Hmm: Bronze Axe is equipped and has 2 in inventory. The candidate set includes 1 Bronze Axe but not the equipped one? maybe keeps one due to equipped.\n\nSo actual eligible set = all equipment items that are not currently equipped (plus dupes of equipped). The UI only displayed 10 rows, total 5428, meaning 13 items. The 3 missing rows (Runite Platebody, Slayer Platebody, Steel Full Helmet) might be below the visible rows but hidden because sheet content scroll, and observe only shows visible elements. But there was a gap between last row and total... Actually the sheet m", "truncated": true}
