{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! With toggle ON, Sell Old Gear candidates collapse to just Bronze Axe ×1 and Iron Sword ×2 — both duplicates of equipped items! It excluded all the armor items (Adamantite, Gilded, Mithril, Runite, etc.) entirely. That seems wrong: keep one of each item should keep one copy of each candidate, not remove all armor candidates. Hmm.\n\nWait maybe \"keep one of each item\" means keep one of each *type*, so armor with x1 each would be kept (not sold) → excluded entirely. That's exactly what happened: items with only 1 in inventory are kept, only duplicates sold (Bronze Axe x2, Iron Sword x3; keep one each → sell 1 and 2). But hold on: is that the intended feature? The label \"Keep one of each item\" suggests when selling, keep one of each item (quantity-wise). So with toggle on, only extras are sold. That's consistent. Then \"Sell Old Gear\" with keep-one will only sell extra copies of equipped gear, not sell old single armor. Hmm, that's logically consistent: keep one of each item cateogry.\n\nBut wait, Sell Old Gear with toggle OFF offered all non-equipped equipment including unique armor. With toggle ON it offers only duplicates of equipped gear. Is that \"correct\"? \"Keep one of each item\" means keep one unit of each item type, so single-unit armor is kept and not sold. Yes plausible.\n\nBut then is there a bug at all? Need to find real defects. Let me focus on changed areas and look for actual inconsistencies. The task expects likely at least one bug per changed area maybe.\n\nLet's examine \"Sell Old Gear\" candidate set more carefully. With toggle OFF, it included equipped items? The equipped Iron Sword is labeled equipped and x3 in inventory; the sheet offered ×2 (keeping the equipped one automatically). Bronze Axe is equipped and x2 inventory; offered ×1. So automatic \"keep equipped copy\". Good. But what about Bronze Pickaxe/Fishing Rod (equipped, count 1) not offered — good.\n\nBut it also offered equipped Bronze Boots? In sell list Bronze Boots equipped ×1; not in old gear (single). With toggle OFF maybe should offer? It was not in sheet first time. Hmm first sheet candidate list included Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger, not Bronze Boots, Bronze Pickaxe, Fishing Rod. So equipped items excluded (except extra copies). That's fine.\n\nNow, \"outdated-equipment bulk action candidate set computed by simplified eligibility filter\": Perhaps the simplified filter is supposed to filter to only items that are actually outdated (worse than equipped/owned best). The fact it includes unique platebodies and Runite Platebody (best) could be the bug: it sells all non-equipped equipment including top-tier. But is that \"outdated\"? Hmm, maybe expected candidate set should only include items worse than the equipped item, and since there's no equipped armor, maybe all armor qualifies? Ambiguous.\n\nLet's look for clues from UI text: button \"Sell Old Gear\". Maybe there's a help/description somewhere. Recent bulk sales maybe shows what was sold.\n\nMaybe test by equipping a new weapon and see if old gear list adjusts. But that changes data; allowed as required. Let's think about how to derive intended behavior. Since \"outdated equipment\" should sell gear that is worse than what you are wearing. With no body armor equipped, any platebody is not \"outdated\" relative to empty, but arguably it's not equipped so it's \"old gear\" (unequipped). Hmm.\n\nAnother angle: Take the changed item \"keep one of each item toggle state restored from save when shop opens.\" Maybe actual bug: after toggling on, exiting via Buy tab and returning to Sell tab shows...? We tested leaving shop and app, persisted. But maybe toggling ON doesn't save immediately? It persisted.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the toggle state restored from save causes the \"Sell Junk\"/\"Sell Old Gear\" behavior to not reflect the toggle on initial open? We saw it does.\n\nLet's test the toggle with a normal individual sale: With keep-one ON, maybe selling from list still allows selling all? Not relevant.\n\nLet's now test quest log, likely easier to spot visual bugs.\n\nQuests bottom nav. Tap Quests (element 30 at 760,2169)."}
