{"type": "thinking", "text": "Journal is notes, not quest log. So quest log = Quests tab. Good.\n\nLet's now focus on finding actual bugs. We have four changes. Let's systematically test each.\n\n### Change 3: Keep one of each item toggle restored from save data when shop opens\n\nWe observed: off initially, toggled on persisted after leaving/reopening and after app restart; toggled off and... did we verify off persists after restart? Maybe. Let's test more thoroughly: toggle on, go Buy tab, return Sell; toggle off, go Buy, back Sell; and kill/reopen. Also check initial saved value is off (matches precondition). There might be a bug where toggle state is saved incorrectly (e.g., after opening, resets to last \"committed\" value). We saw it persisted. Maybe the bug is that the settinn is only persisted when Sell tab open, or restoring after app restart might not work if it was toggled and app killed quickly. Low likelihood.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the toggle shows checked but is not applied on the initial open (we tested Sell Junk after toggling on while already on screen, applied). After reopening with on, did we test Sell Junk? We toggled on, left, reopened (checked), then toggled off before testing Sell Junk. So we haven't verified that the restored ON state is actually applied to bulk actions when shop opens. Let's test: set ON, leave shop, reopen, go Sell, open Sell Junk, expect quantities-1. This could reveal a bug (switch shows ON but internal flag false, or vice versa).\n\nLet's do that later.\n\n### Change 2: Sell Old Gear candidate set\n\nWe need expected. Maybe look at \"Recent bulk sales\" after a sale to see details. That could help infer. But don't want to change data too much; though selling is part of shop testing and allowed. We can test with small items.\n\nIdea: The \"simplified eligibility filter\" may have a clear bug: it includes *equipped* items. Wait it included Bronze Axe which is equipped, and Iron Sword equipped. Actually with toggle off, it offered Bronze Axe ×1 while inventory has Bronze Axe ×2 and it's equipped. The equipped copy should be excluded; extra copies are eligible, so ×1 correct. Iron Sword ×3 equipped → ×2 correct. So it properly handles equipped duplicates.\n\nBut it also included *Agility Cape* and *Mercantile Cape* — these are capes, possibly \"equipment\" but non-combat? They might be cosmetic. It included *Bronze Dagger* (weapon) while Iron Sword equipped → outdated indeed. Included *Adamantite/Gilded/Mithril/Runite Chainbody* while no body armor equipped; if no body armor equipped, they're not \"outdated\" but could be \"old\" (unused). Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe expected candidate set is \"items that are NOT currently equipped\" (i.e., sell everything not equipped), which is exactly what we see. Then no bug. But then why \"simplified eligibility filter\" change note? They might have deliberately changed to something buggy, e.g., filter checks `item.sellable` only. Hmm.\n\nLet's check whether any items that should be eligible are missing. Inventory includes:\n- Bronze Pickaxe x1 (equipped) — not eligible.\n- Bronze Axe x2 (equipped) — eligible extra 1. yes.\n- Bronze Fishing Rod x1 (equipped) — not.\n- Bronze Boots x1 (equipped) — not.\n- Iron Sword x3 (equipped) — eligible extra 2. yes.\n- Bronze Dagger x1 — eligible. yes.\n- Agility Cape x1 — eligible. yes.\n- Mithril Platebody x1 — eligible. yes.\n- Adamantite Platebody x1 — eligible. yes.\n- Slayer Platebody x1 — eligible (in scroll).\n- Runite Chainbody x1 — eligible. yes.\n- Runite Platebody x1 — eligible (in scroll).\n- Gilded Platebody x1 — eligible. yes.\n- Steel Full Helmet x1 — eligible (in scroll).\n- Mithril Med Helmet x1 — eligible. yes.\n\nSo all non-equipped equippable items are eligible. That is \"sell all unused gear\". Plausible intended.\n\nMaybe the bug: The candidate set should exclude the *best* item for each slot (to avoid selling upgrades). \"Outdated equipment\" semantics = worse than current best. Then candidates should be: platebodies worse than Runite Platebody (Mithril, Adamantite, Gilded, Slayer, Runite Chainbody?), helmets worse than Mithril Med? maybe Steel Full Helmet should be sold; weapons worse than Iron Sword (Bronze Dagger, Bronze Axe? Bronze Axe is a tool/war axe?), capes: Agility/Mercantile maybe compared. But the app includes the best platebody Runite and best helmet Mithril Med, excludes Steel Full Helmet (worse!). This asymmetry could indicate a real bug in the simplified filter: perhaps it compares by item *name* or *tier index* incorrectly.\n\nLet me get the stats of these armors to determine which are better. Equip screen or item detail might show. Let's check Combat screen equipment stats. Actually inventory item details might show stats when tapped in shop sell? Let's tap an item? It might sell immediately (danger). In sell list, tapping item likely opens quantity sheet, not immediate. Could inspect stats maybe not.\n\nMaybe the \"My House\"/inventory? Profile? Let's open Profile and see inventory with GE values/stats.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Combat screen shows equipment. Let's check Combat to see currently equipped and stats of owned items. But likely not list all.\n\nLet's open profile."}
