{"type": "thinking", "text": "No Stone. So Stone not in Smithing.\n\nMaybe Construction skill (not in Skills list) uses Stone to craft Carved Stone. The Builder's Workshop \"Carved Stone\" material is likely crafted from Stone via a \"Construction\" recipe accessible in Builder's Workshop \"Upgrade\" flow? The upgrade requires Carved Stone, not raw Stone. But there must be a way to obtain Carved Stone, likely from a Stone recipe in Construction. Since Construction skill isn't in Skills list, maybe My House/Builder's Workshop has a crafting interface not visible because we can't upgrade. Hmm.\n\nWait maybe Construction recipes are in the \"Crafting\" skill but only visible with \"Only craftable\" off? We had Only craftable off (it was a toggle). The list was jewellery only. Hmm.\n\nMaybe \"Stone\" is used in \"Smithing\" as an ingredient for \"Furnace\" etc. beyond our level. The category \"Armour/Bar/Component/Tool\" might include \"Furnace\" in \"Component\" under higher tiers? We saw all component items for Mithril only; there could be more below (Adamantite, Runite). Let's scroll component further. Could include \"Stone\" as a component? Unlikely.\n\nAlternatively, \"Stone\" might be used in \"Runecrafting\" to craft runes? Runes use essence. Hmm.\n\nLet's test Sell Junk after buying a \"Stone\" from shop? Already have 12. The list excludes it. The change note says \"which items count as useful is now decided from crafting recipes.\" If Stone is not in any recipe, that's a bug. But we can't conclusively prove from UI (we can't see construction recipes).\n\nMaybe the bug is instead with **Copper Ore / Tin Ore**: they're used in Smithing Bronze Bar → excluded (correct). **Logs** used in Fletching/Firemaking → excluded (correct). **Stone** used in Construction (Carved Stone) → excluded (correct). Junk items: Cowhide, Feather, Pumpkin, Tomato, Wool — maybe all genuinely unused. So Sell Junk seems correct. Maybe the bug is that it excludes **Feather**? Wait Feather IS used in Fletching in RuneScape, and the app's Fletching description might use feathers for arrows. But the recipe list showed Bronze Arrows using \"Arrow Shafts 0/15 Bronze Arrow Tips 0/15\" — no Feather. Maybe higher-tier arrows use feathers? Let's check Iron Arrows recipe. Fletching items list after Bronze Arrows might include Iron Arrows etc. Scroll down. But they likely use Iron Arrow Tips. Hmm.\n\nLet's inspect Fletching further down to see if any recipe uses Feather. Tap Fletching and scroll. We'll check Iron/Steel arrows, bows, planks. If a recipe uses Feather, then Sell Junk including Feather is a bug. This is a promising bug because Feather is a classic arrow component and the item description may say \"Used in Fletching.\" Let's check item description in shop: Feather description? In sell list, Feather has no description. In buy list maybe \"Feather\" not sold? Let's check via search. Actually the shop Buy list may have Feather in MISC section. Could show description \"Used in Fletching to make arrows.\" Let's search buy list later.\n\nFirst check Fletching recipes. Back, Fletching."}
