{"type": "thinking", "text": "No feathers. So Feather is not used in Fletching recipes. It might be used in Fishing (bait?) or Cooking? Let's check item description for Feather. In Sell list, item rows don't show description. In Buy tab maybe items have descriptions. Search \"Feather\" in shop search box. Buy tab search? The search exists in Sell tab only. Buy list may have Feather somewhere in \"MISC\". Let's use Sell search? That shows sell price only. Hmm.\n\nMaybe Profile → Inventory? There's no inventory screen; shop sell is inventory.\n\nLet's check the buy list for Feather description. The Buy tab is very long but searchable? There is no search on Buy. Could scroll to misc section (much further). Alternatively the item's description may appear on tap purchase sheet. In Sell list, tapping item opens sell quantity sheet, maybe with description. Let's tap Feather in sell list to see sheet. That could show description \"Used for...\" and maybe sell options. Let's do it; cancel after.\n\nGo Shop -> Sell, scroll to Feather, tap. But maybe quicker: search \"Feather\" in shop sell search. Then tap row to open sheet. Let's do. Navigate Home→Shop first (currently in Fletching sheet). Back, then shop.\n\nActually, I realize we should prioritize finding the seeded bugs. Let's consider likely bug design. Each changed feature might have a bug that is *observable via the UI with the given preconditions*. Let's list candidate defects we've noticed:\n\nA. Quest log completed rows still show \"Go to Skill\" button (maybe intended).\nB. Quest log/Sell Junk potential misclassification (uncertain).\nC. Sell Old Gear includes all non-equipped gear including best upgrades (uncertain).\nD. Toggle restore maybe fine.\nE. Guild Hall \"4 left today\" vs 3 completed dailies (uncertain).\nF. \"Equip Best Gear\" isn't changed.\n\nMaybe there are bugs not related to changes: e.g., buying the XP boost with 2.5M coins; special item price display \"1.8M coins\" strikethrough \"2.5M coins\" maybe discount. Buying could deduct 1.8M. Not in changed list but shop area. Could be a bug there (e.g., wrong price). Let's test shop purchase flow maybe.\n\nBut the instruction: sweep the shop and quest log. So bugs could be anywhere in these.\n\nLet's systematically test the shop:\n- Buy item (e.g., Logs) quantity flow, coin deduction, inventory increment.\n- Sell item individually, coin increment, inventory decrement, equipped guard.\n- Sell Junk and Sell Old Gear flows.\n- Keep one toggle.\n- Filters/search/sorting.\n- Recent bulk sales.\n- Special XP boost purchase maybe limit one per week.\n\nAnd quest log:\n- Tabs, hide completed, go to skill, reset, progress display, completion display, rewards.\n- Quest board via guild hall daily requests and quest list.\n- Rotation.\n\nLet's begin with shop Buy flow: buy something cheap, e.g., Copper Ore 3 coins? Actually we have 40; buy 1 Tin Ore? Let's buy a cheap item and verify coin deduction. Coin display shows \"2.5M\" rounded; hard to verify small changes. Use a more expensive item to see coins change, e.g., Basic Staff 375 or 2× XP Boost 1.8M. Better: buy \"Necklace of Anguish\" 2.2M? That would change coins display to maybe 300K, clearly visible—but huge data change and irreversible. We can sell it back at lower price, losing money, but data integrity not critical. Yet risky. Maybe buy Basic Staff 375, coins still 2.5M rounded, no visible. But then sell it back at 93? We can't see.\n\nAlternatively use Sell flow: sell a high-value item (Runite Platebody 1250) — coins still rounded 2.5M. Not visible.\n\nMaybe Profile shows exact coins? Home shows \"2.5M\". Profile maybe exact. Let's check Profile. It may show exact coin count 2,567,890. That could verify transactions. Let's open Profile."}
