{"type": "thinking", "text": "Inventory shows Iron Sword x3, Bronze Dagger x1, Bronze Boots x1, Agility Cape x1, Mithril Platebody, Adamantite Platebody, Slayer Platebody, Runite Chainbody, Runite Platebody... Wait! Gilded Platebody is missing from inventory because it's equipped (not counted in inventory list). Steel Full Helmet equipped, also missing. Good.\n\nBut notice: \"Agility Cape\" still x1 in inventory even though equipped? Earlier Equip Best Gear equipped Agility Cape. Shop sell list showed \"Agility Cape (equipped) ×1 in inventory\". Hmm, so equipped items still counted in inventory? Profile inventory shows Agility Cape x1 (maybe includes equipped). Iron Sword x3 includes equipped one. So inventory counts include equipped items. Fine.\n\nThe inventory screen is useful: search items, sort, categories. Could use it to inspect item counts before/after shop transactions.\n\nAlso note \"Bronze Pickaxe\" and \"Bronze Axe\" and \"Bronze Fishing Rod\" are not in the visible inventory list? Maybe under Tools category. We can filter Tools.\n\nNo exact coins though, still 2.5M.\n\nHmm, no exact coin display anywhere. So transaction verification relies on rounded display. Could use big transactions.\n\nLet's think about the shop bug candidates again. Maybe there's a bug where **selling an equipped item through the sell list** is allowed and strips equipment. In sell list, equipped items show \"(equipped)\" and tapping could sell them. Precondition has equipped Iron Sword, Bronze Pickaxe, etc. Does individual sell guard against selling equipped? Let's test carefully: tap Iron Sword (equipped) row and see the sell sheet; it may offer quantities including the equipped one. If selling all would leave you unequipped, maybe that's intended? Usually shouldn't sell equipped copy. But the row shows \"(equipped) ×3 in inventory\" and old gear sheet kept 1 (implicitly the equipped one). Individual sale might allow selling all 3? Let's check the quantity sheet's max. This could