{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"No bulk sales recorded yet.\" After an individual sale, fine (bulk only). Good.\n\nNow maybe test bulk sale with actual transaction? Could sell junk with keep-one off, which changes data. It's okay, but maybe we can test and then check recent bulk sales. This is the shop area and likely where bug lurks. Let's consider that the bulk sale might credit wrong total or not remove items correctly. Testing with Sell Junk (5 items) would remove most crafting materials; that's a large permanent change, but we can compare and maybe rebuy some. Since our task is QA, allowed. It could reveal a bug (e.g., \"keep one\" ignored, or total wrong). The benchmark likely wants us to test these actions.\n\nBut before destructive tests, let's try to identify the seeded bug from static observations.\n\nShop Sell Old Gear with toggle ON showed only duplicates (Bronze Axe ×1, Iron Sword ×2) — but wait, this was *before* we sold an Iron Sword. At that time Iron Sword x3 and sold 2 would leave 1. Fine.\n\nI want to test \"Sell Old Gear\" after equipping a *weak* body to see if better gear is listed. Let's do this controlled test now, then restore Gilded afterward:\n1. Go Combat→Gear→Body→equip Mithril Platebody.\n2. Shop→Sell→Sell Old Gear (toggle off).\n3. Check whether Gilded Platebody (Def 95) appears in candidates while Mithril (Def 48) equipped.\nIf yes, report as bug: bulk sells upgrades.\nBut is that really a bug? Let's think like a game designer: \"Sell Old Gear\" bulk sells items that are strictly worse than the currently equipped item in each slot. Equipping Mithril while owning Gilded is unusual (player choice), but a safe \"sell old gear\" shouldn't sell the Gilded upgrade. I'd call it a bug.\n\nHowever, the change note \"simplified eligibility filter\" could mean they intentionally simplified to \"all unequipped equipment\" and the bug is something else, e.g., it erroneously *excludes* the best. Hmm.\n\nLet's do the test and see.\n\nBut wait—equipping a weaker body might auto-equip? Body slot shows alternatives; selecting Mithril will unequip Gilded. Then Sell Old Gear list. Let's proceed. Navigate Combat (bottom x=320,y=2169) then Gear tab, Body, Mithril.\n\nCurrent screen is shop sell. Press back twice to return? Use bottom nav Combat requires leaving shop. Press back arrow element 20 maybe then wait. Let's just press BACK to home (maybe two times)."}
