{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reset worked: Fishing I no longer shows Completed or Reset; it now shows just title/desc/Go to Skill. It's at top and appears incomplete. There was no confirmation dialog? It reset immediately. Also notice rows shifted. This seems fine.\n\nBut wait, did the quest completion actually reset and the row update? Yes.\n\nHmm, but now we've lost a completed quest. Fine.\n\nInteresting: After reset, the row's \"Completed\" and \"Reset\" are gone. Good.\n\nMaybe tap Reset again? Not needed.\n\nLet's consider a possible bug: After resetting, the quest progress resets to 0 but **does it also remove the completed status globally**? Not relevant.\n\nNow check if Hide completed filtering works after reset—yes, Fishing I now appears even with hide completed off. With hide completed on, it should appear too. Not a bug.\n\nWe need to find the seeded bug. Let's revisit the changed items and think about what could be subtly wrong:\n\n**Quest log row component**: Maybe the row shows the \"Go to Skill\" button even for completed quests (we saw that). If the correct row component for the quest log should hide \"Go to Skill\" when completed, that's a minor UI bug. But the shared component with the quest board would also show it. Hmm.\n\nWait, look at the completed row in the screenshot: \"Fishing I\" title, \"Go to Skill\" at right, then \"Completed\" and \"Reset\". In the quest board (guild quests), locked quests show title with lock, description, \"Requires Guild Level X\", and \"Go to Skill\" even though locked. Maybe the board always shows \"Go to Skill\". Shared component makes sense.\n\nMaybe the bug is that the quest log's **progress bar is missing for incomplete quests**? In Daily/Weekly, incomplete quests show progress bars (0/80). In Gathering, incomplete quests (Fishing II, Mining II, Thieving I, Woodcutting II) show no progress bar! Compare: Daily Salmon Griller shows ProgressBar and 0/80; Gathering Fishing II shows only title/desc/Go to Skill, no progress bar. Is that a bug? These are one-time quests; maybe progress bars only for dailies/weeklies, not achievements. Could be intended.\n\nBut wait: The changed row component shared with quest board — the quest board rows for daily requests show progress bars. Quest log rows for Gathering achievements might not have progress. Hmm.\n\nMaybe one of the *dailies* has a completed state to check. None completed. Could complete a daily? Hard (Cook 80 salmon). Not feasible.\n\n**Outdated equipment**: We observed the filter includes gear not \"best\" but not the best; this might be intended.\n\nWait, actually let's test \"Sell Old Gear\" with toggle OFF and *no armor equipped* again. It included the best Gilded Platebody. Under \"sell all non-best gear\", Gilded is best → should be excluded, but it was included! In our first test (before Equip Best Gear), no body equipped, and Gilded was in the list. Later after equipping Mithril, Gilded was excluded. So the filter's \"best\" computation appears to depend on equipped state? Hmm, let's re-examine:\n\nTest 1 (no body armor equipped): candidates included Gilded, Adamantite, Slayer, Runite Platebody, Runite Chain, Mithril, Mithril Med, Steel Full, Agility Cape, Mercantile Cape, Bronze Dagger, Bronze Axe. Actually the full candidate set was all equipment (Sum 5428 included all). So with empty slots, everything is eligible. That matches \"sell all non-equipped\" or \"candidate = item not equipped\" without any best protection.\n\nTest 2 (Gilded equipped): candidates excluded Gilded/Steel/Agility (equipped) and included all remaining armor.\n\nTest 3 (Mithril equipped): candidates included all remaining armor EXCEPT Gilded — wait, but Gilded was not equipped. Why excluded?? Did we maybe still have Gilded equipped in another loadout? No. Let's verify inventory has Gilded. Hmm, maybe the Mithril equip didn't actually unequip Gilded? It did (body shows Mithril, DEF 144 from 191). Gilded should be in inventory. Why not in Sell Old Gear? Could it be that Sell Old Gear **only considers items up to a certain inventory order/limit** and Gilded is off-screen? But total 4217 exactly equals displayed items (we computed). Let me recompute total 4217: 937+25+25+62+6+437+1250+1250+225 = let's sum: 937+25=962, +25=987, +62=1049, +6=1055, +437=1492, +1250=2742, +1250=3992, +225=4217. Yes exactly. So Gilded absent.\n\nWait—did we sell Gilded earlier inadvertently? No, we never bulk sold old gear. We only sold 1 Iron Sword and junk. Could \"Equip Best Gear\" have *consumed* the Gilded? No, equip just moves to equipped slot; inventory list earlier after equipping did not show Gilded (because equipped). Then we equipped Mithril, so Gilded should return to inventory. But maybe the game treats equipment switching such that the previously equipped Gilded is dropped/lost? That would be a bug! Let's check Profile Inventory now for Gilded count. If Gilded is missing entirely from inventory after switching from Gilded to Mithril, that's a serious bug (item loss). But more likely I misread and Gilded excluded from old-gear sheet because... hmm.\n\nActually wait: maybe when we tapped \"Mithril Platebody\" in Choose Body, the sheet selection **equipped Mithril but removed Gilded from inventory because it was already equipped**? No, switching should put Gilded back.\n\nLet's check Profile Inventory. It's important. Navigate Profile→Inventory and search Gilded / scroll. Do it after this.\n\nAlso note: Sell Old Gear after Gilded equipped (test 2) excluded Agility Cape (equipped) and included Mercantile Cape. Fine.\n\nLet's verify Gilded count. Navigate Profile. Tap x=980,y=2169 then wait, Inventory [11], search maybe \"Gilded\". Let's do."}
