{"type": "thinking", "text": "Gilded Platebody ×1 exists in inventory. So why is it missing from Sell Old Gear when Mithril equipped? Let's re-open Sell Old Gear with Mithril equipped and toggle off, and verify the list again carefully, maybe scroll the sheet to reveal Gilded below. The sheet list is scrollable; we saw 9 rows + total. Maybe Gilded was below the visible rows! Let's scroll the sheet. Earlier we assumed total equals displayed sum; but maybe total includes hidden items and coincidence? Wait total 4217 exactly matched 9 displayed. But with hidden Gilded (300), total would be 4517. It showed 4217. Hmm, unless Gilded is excluded from total because... no.\n\nBut maybe the sheet's displayed list was scrolled at some position, hiding some items above too. The first item was Adamantite at top. Hidden items maybe below, and total includes all candidates (including hidden) — we computed total matched displayed exactly, which would be a coincidence? Let's recompute displayed list at that time: Adamantite 937, Bronze Axe 25, Bronze Dagger 25, Iron Sword 62, Mercantile Cape 6, Mithril Med Helmet 437, Runite Chainbody 1250, Runite Platebody 1250, Slayer Platebody 225 = 4217. If Gilded were also included, total would be 4517. So it is excluded. Unless the Gilded \"sell price\" is 0? No, earlier sell list showed Gilded 300 coins.\n\nSo why would Sell Old Gear exclude Gilded when Mithril equipped? Maybe because Gilded is considered the \"best gear\" and protected (regardless of equipped). Then when Gilded was equipped, Runite Platebody etc. were included (not best). And when no armor equipped, was Gilded included? In the first test before Equip Best Gear, total 5428 = includes Gilded 300. That suggests with nothing equipped, Gilded was NOT protected. Hmm contradiction.\n\nWait maybe in the first test, the item list was different: it included Adamantite, Agility Cape, Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger, Gilded, Iron Sword x2, Mercantile Cape, Mithril Med Helmet, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody... total 5428 which included hidden Runite Platebody, Slayer, Steel Full. Let's recompute if Gilded were excluded from first list: displayed sum without Gilded = 3735-300=3435; plus hidden Runite Plate (1250)+Slayer(225)+Steel(218)=1693 → 5128, not 5428. So Gilded was definitely included in the first test (5428). So no blanket \"best item\" protection.\n\nThen why excluded when Mithril equipped? Let's think: Maybe \"candidate set\" is items that are **not currently equipped AND not the item you last equipped via 'Equip Best Gear'?** No. Or maybe Gilded is **locked**? No.\n\nHmm, maybe when we switched body from Gilded to Mithril, the Gilded Platebody became the *equipped item in the \"Equip Best Gear\" saved loadout* and the old-gear filter excludes it as \"best\". The filter might compute \"best gear\" including the Gilded (best by def) and exclude it when another item is equipped? In first test, no armor equipped → best gear for body maybe \"None\", so Gilded wasn't identified as best? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the old gear filter is: candidate = equipped? no... Let's compare candidate sets:\n- State A: body=None, head=None, cape=None (original). Candidates = all equipment items (except equipped tools? Actually all non-equipped equipment incl. the best).\n- State B: body=Gilded, head=Steel, cape=Agility. Candidates = all non-equipped equipment (excluded equipped).\n- State C: body=Mithril, head=Steel, cape=Agility. Candidates = all non-equipped equipment EXCEPT Gilded.\n\nMaybe in State C, Gilded is actually still considered \"equipped\" in the character's *saved equipment* due to a bug/async state? But Combat Gear showed Mithril as equipped and DEF 144, and Gilded in inventory. So no.\n\nMaybe the Sell Old Gear sheet **was scrolled** and Gilded is in the hidden part above? Let's re-open and scroll the sheet to be sure. The sheet's visible list at state C: first item Adamantite; maybe Gilded was above (hidden) but total only 4217? Hmm if Gilded hidden above, total would include it. Unless total is computed for visible list only? No.\n\nLet's test again with Mithril still equipped: open Sell Old Gear, inspect, then scroll the sheet. Maybe I'll learn more. Navigate shop. It's worth confirming because if the filter protects the *best* item only when something is equipped, that's weird.\n\nActually, maybe I mis-assigned which item is which. In state C, maybe Gilded was not \"in inventory\" at that time because our equip action hadn't committed? But we checked later it is in inventory. Could there be a timing issue: We equipped Mithril, then immediately opened Sell Old Gear maybe before the game updated Gilded's inventory state? Unlikely, plenty of steps in between (navigate home, shop, sell tab).\n\nLet's repeat now: Profile search shows Gilded x1. Go Shop Sell Old Gear (toggle off), inspect list, scroll."}
