{"type": "thinking", "text": "Gilded row: \"Gilded Platebody | ×1 in inventory | 300 coins ea.\" No \"(locked)\" or \"(equipped)\". So it's sellable individually. Yet excluded from Sell Old Gear. This is a candidate bug: the bulk \"Sell Old Gear\" candidate set excludes an item that is neither equipped nor locked. But why? Maybe because Gilded is the \"best\" body armor in inventory, and the filter intentionally excludes best-in-slot. But then why include Runite Platebody (second best) and all lower? That's exactly \"exclude best-in-slot\". So the filter is \"sell all equipment except the best item per slot (and equipped)\". That's plausible. Is that \"outdated equipment\"? It would include gear better than current equipped (state C), which could be dangerous but perhaps intended because \"best loadout\" is computed independent of current equip. When we equipped Mithril (a downgrade), the bulk action still protects Gilded as the best item. So from a \"sell old gear\" perspective, the candidate set is \"everything not in your best loadout\", excluding gear that's part of your best gear set. That's actually sensible and safe: you won't accidentally sell your best armor even if currently wearing something else. So no bug.\n\nBut wait, in state A (nothing equipped), Gilded was included, which contradicts \"exclude best item per slot\". Unless in state A the \"best gear\" computation for body returned *Mithril Platebody* or something else? Let's check: In state A, no body equipped. Equip Best Gear chose Gilded, so Gilded is best. If filter excluded best, Gilded should be absent from candidates. But it was present. Hmm. Unless the state A observation had a different toggle ON? Let's recall: First Sell Old Gear opened when toggle was OFF (screenshot showed off). Yes.\n\nWait, maybe I mis-summed and Gilded was NOT in the first sheet. Let me re-read the first observation. It listed:\nAdamantite, ×1, 937\nAgility Cape ×1 6\nBronze Axe ×1 25\nBronze Dagger ×1 25\nGilded Platebody ×1 300\nIron Sword ×2 124\nMercantile Cape ×1 6\nMithril Med Helmet ×1 437\nMithril Platebody ×1 625\nRunite Chainbody ×1 1,250\nTotal 5,428\n\nYes Gilded listed. Sum 3735 + hidden 1693 (Runite Plate 1250, Slayer 225, Steel Full 218) = 5428. But wait hidden items were inferred, not observed! Could the hidden 1693 be something else? Let's check test 3 total 4217 and items: Adamantite 937, Bronze Axe 25, Bronze Dagger 25, Iron Sword 62, Mercantile 6, Mithril Med 437, Runite Chain 1250, Runite Plate 1250, Slayer 225 = 4217. So in state C, Runite Platebody is visible (y=1829) — no hidden. In state A, the visible list ended at Runite Chainbody with total 5428, implying hidden items totaling 1693. If Gilded (300) somehow appears in state C list? no. Hmm.\n\nWait, in state A, the inventory was different? At state A, we had not equipped anything and had *not sold* 1 Iron Sword yet. Iron Sword was x3, so old gear offered x2 = 124 (same). Agility Cape was x1, etc.\n\nMaybe the hidden items in state A were **Bronze Boots, Bronze Pickaxe, Bronze Fishing Rod** (equipped, should be excluded) plus **???**. Sum Bronze Boots 10 + Pickaxe 25 + Rod 20 = 55. Not 1693.\n\nWhat combination of items sums to 1693? Runite Platebody 1250 + Slayer 225 + Steel Full 218 = 1693 exactly. Strong evidence. Those three were hidden in state A's scroll list, and Gilded was visible. So Gilded was included in state A.\n\nWhy would Gilded be included in state A but excluded in state C? Maybe the filter excludes **currently equipped items plus the item that's equipped in the \"best gear\" *set* only when a slot has something equipped**? Hmm. Actually here's a plausible algorithm: For each equipment slot, determine \"best owned item\" via def/attack value. Exclude that best item only if there is at least one item equipped in that slot? That seems arbitrary.\n\nAlternative: The filter excludes items whose **defense is >= the equipped item's defense** when a slot is equipped, but includes items with **defense > equipped** when no item equipped? In state C, Gilded 95 > Mithril 48, should be excluded; Adamantite 66 > 48 also should be excluded but included. Not it.\n\nMaybe the filter uses **sell value** rather than defense and excludes items with sell value > equipped item's sell value? State C equipped Mithril sells 625; Gilded 300 < 625, so not excluded by value. no.\n\nMaybe the item's **tier** vs equipped: equipped Mithril (tier?), exclude items of equal or higher tier? Adamantite higher, included. no.\n\nHmm.\n\nMaybe Gilded is excluded because it is **the last item equipped via 'Equip Best Gear' and still flagged as \"reserved\"**? Could be a bug where swapping equipment leaves the old item in an \"equippedItems\" set, so it's still considered equipped for the filter even though UI shows Mithril. Then:\n- State A: nothing equipped → Gilded not in equipped set → included.\n- State B: Equip Best Gear equips Gilded → equipped set contains Gilded.\n- State C: swap body to Mithril → UI equipped set should be {Mithril}, but perhaps old Gilded remains in the set used by the sell filter → excluded. That would be a real bug: after changing equipment, the previous item remains \"equipped\" in the sell filter, so it won't be offered for sale. But is that harmful? It just excludes an item from bulk sale incorrectly. It's a \"missing item from candidate list\" bug. Could report.\n\nBut maybe the exclusion is intentional: \"Sell Old Gear\" might exclude the **best-in-slot item** when any gear is equipped, because that's the \"best setup\". Hmm.\n\nLet's test state D: equip a *different* item, e.g., Runite Platebody (def 90), and check whether Gilded (95, now unequipped) is still excluded and whether Mithril (48, previously equipped) appears. If Mithril appears and Gilded remains excluded, that suggests \"best-in-slot protection\" independent of equip. If Mithril is excluded (stale equipped) and Gilded appears, that suggests stale-equipped bug.\n\nLet's do controlled test:\n- Equip Runite Platebody.\n- Open Sell Old Gear (toggle off).\n- Check: Mithril Platebody should be included (it's worse), Gilded should be excluded (best). If Mithril missing → stale equipped set bug. If Gilded missing but Mithril present → best-in-slot exclusion.\nEarlier state C: Mithril equipped, Gilded excluded, other better items included. If best-in-slot, that's \"protect Gilded\". Let's test.\n\nActually, we can also equip a *worse* head or something. But body test suffices.\n\nLet's equip Runite Platebody. Currently shop sell with search Gilded. Navigate Combat→Gear→Body→Runite Platebody. Then shop old gear.\n\nDo it. Tap Combat at (320,2169) then wait."}
