{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! Fishing Guild Quests tab shows \"Shrimp Haul\" Completed, but guild level 0 and 0/2 dailies. Also \"4 left today\" in Guild Hall. Now let's check Daily Requests tab: maybe Shrimp Haul is a permanent quest (not daily), completed. The fact \"4 left today\" could be correct for daily requests, but \"0/2 dailies\" suggests no daily requests completed this day. The precondition says \"guild quests Copper Run, Iron Quota and Shrimp Haul (3 guild quests)\" — these appear to be permanent quests (under \"Quests\" tab), not daily requests. So Shrimp Haul completed is shown correctly. Good. Mining Guild likely Copper Run/Iron Quota completed under Quests tab. Let's verify Mining Guild. But likely fine.\n\nGuild \"Level 0\" with completed Shrimp Haul? The guild level progress says 0/2 dailies, but permanent quests may not affect guild level; only daily requests do. So fine.\n\nNow, important: The Fishing Guild quest list shows completed Shrimp Haul row with **\"Go to Skill\" button and \"Completed\" but no Reset button**! Wait, compare with Quest log completed rows (Fishing I etc.) which had a \"Reset\" button. Here Shrimp Haul completed row shows no Reset. Why? Maybe guild quests aren't repeatable, so no Reset. Let's look: element [6] Shrimp Haul, [7] Go to Skill, [8] desc, [9] Completed icon, [10] Completed. No Reset. So guild completed quests don't show Reset; quest log ones do. That's a difference but maybe intentional (guild quests are one-time).\n\nHmm. The changed \"quest rows built from new row component shared with the quest board\" — if the shared component is used in both, why does the quest log completed row show Reset but guild completed row doesn't? Maybe the Reset button is an extra passed in only for quest log. Fine.\n\nNow, check \"Hide completed\" toggle state: It's off here (unchecked) though we toggled it on in quest log and then off. It's shared global state maybe. Fine.\n\nNow, let's tap \"Go to Skill\" on the completed Shrimp Haul. Should navigate to Fishing. Works likely.\n\nLet's inspect Daily Requests tab of Fishing Guild: if Shrimp Haul was a daily request, maybe it's not there. The daily requests names would be different. Precondition says Shrimp Haul is a guild quest (permanent). OK.\n\nAt this point I haven't found a definitive bug. Let's scrutinize the quest log rows for **wrong progress**:\n- Precondition: Mining I completed \"Mine 500 Copper Ore\" — correct.\n- Fishing I completed \"Catch 500 fish\" — correct.\n- Woodcutting I \"Cut 500 Logs\" — correct.\n- Smithing I \"Smelt 500 Bronze Bars\" — correct.\nThese match typical thresholds.\n- Precondition smithing level 19 with 4,400 XP. Smithing I shows Completed.\n- Woodcutting II says \"Cut 750 Oak Logs\" — plausible.\n- Mining II \"Mine 750 Iron Ore\" — plausible.\n- Fishing II \"Catch 750 fish\" — plausible.\n\nWhat about **completed quests count**? The \"Quests\" tab maybe shows a count badge \"Skills (1)\"? On Skills tab it said \"Skills (1)\" with quest icons. Hmm, that \"1\" might indicate one active quest? Let's explore that: Skills tab header \"Skills (1)\" maybe means 1 completed? Not sure. Also \"Quest icons\" toggle. The quest icon indicators (⚒️⁴, ⏰) on skills could show quest states. Might be buggy: Mining shows \"⚒️⁴\" (4 quests?), Fishing \"⚒️⁴\", Cooking \"⏰\" and \"..\". Could indicate active quest counts. Not in scope maybe.\n\nMaybe the quest log bug is with **progress display on partial progress**. All our visible quest progress is 0. Could we create partial progress? We could start a combat/skill session to accumulate progress, then check quest log. That would test progress bars. E.g., start Mining session for a few seconds, then check Mining II progress? But the quest \"Mine 750 Iron Ore\" requires iron ore and we have no iron ore; mining might yield copper/tin. Not easy. We could do Fishing (Shrimp) maybe. But time.\n\nGiven the task, maybe I should look for obvious defects via screenshots of each quest tab. Let's examine the Daily/Weekly rows more closely for layout issues (cut-off text, overlapping). The screenshot of Gathering looked fine.\n\nMaybe the bug is: **Completed quest rows still show the \"Go to Skill\" button, which overlaps the row divider or is misaligned**—no.\n\nCould be the **\"Reset\" button on completed quest rows is missing the \"Completed\" progress bar**—not.\n\nLet's test the \"Hide completed\" toggle combined with the quest log rows. When hide completed is ON, the list correctly excludes. But the tab count/other data? Fine.\n\nWhat about **navigating to quest log from multiple routes**: bottom nav Quests, Skills \"Quest icons\", etc. Maybe one route shows a different category or stale data. The Skills screen has \"Quest icons\" toggle top right, which shows icons on skill cards. Tapping a quest icon might navigate to quest log? Not sure.\n\nLet's check the \"Quest icons\" toggle on Skills. It's checked by default. If we tap it, icons hide. Fine.\n\nMaybe the quest log tab **doesn't remember scroll/tab** when leaving and returning; not necessarily bug.\n\nLet's look at the Weekly header: \"Complete all 5 to earn a bonus: 100,000 coins, or a 3.8% chance at a piece of Divine gear.\" The five weekly quests are visible. Fine.\n\nDaily header: \"Each daily quest rewards coins. Every quest also has a 1 in 100 chance to drop a piece of Dwarven gear you don't own yet. Each claim without a drop improves the odds; a drop resets them to 1 in 100.\" But there's no way to claim: rows show only \"Go to Skill\" and progress; at 0/80 no claim. At completion, perhaps a \"Claim\" button appears. We can't test.\n\nHmm.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is in the **quest log's completed quest reward/Reset**: Tapping \"Reset\" resets but perhaps should reset only for repeatable quests, and it may reset the wrong data (e.g., resets XP? no).\n\nWait—after we reset Fishing I, did the *guild quest* or other screen reflect? Let's check if Fishing I completion is still counted elsewhere (e.g., Skills \"Quests\" icon, or Profile Achievements). Not important.\n\nLet's consider the possibility that the four changed items are *not* all buggy. The benchmark may have one or two bugs. We must find them.\n\nMaybe the bugs are in places we haven't tested:\n- \"Keep one of each item toggle state restored from save data when the shop opens.\" We verified on/off persistence across shop reopen and app background. But maybe **the checkbox is restored only on the Sell tab, not when the Shop opens on Buy**; the requirement says \"when the shop opens\" — we reopen to Buy, then go Sell and the state is correct. That seems fine. Could there be a bug that the toggle **resets to the saved state when returning from Buy to Sell** even if changed? e.g., toggle on Sell, switch to Buy, switch back to Sell → does it keep the new state or revert to saved? We haven't tested. Let's test: On Sell, toggle ON (currently saved OFF). Switch to Buy, back to Sell, observe. If it reverts to OFF, that's a bug: state not kept within session. We should test. Good idea.\n\nAlso test: toggle ON, switch to Buy, switch back, maybe it shows ON. Then exit shop and reopen—it should persist (saved). We did that.\n\nLet's test tab switch now. Currently in Fishing Guild (not shop). Navigate Home→Shop→Sell, toggle ON, switch Buy, back Sell, observe. Need be efficient.\n\nActually, we can test by observing the toggle state after tab switching. Let's do it.\n\nNavigate Home (540,2169) -> wait -> Shop [9] -> Sell [1] -> toggle [7] -> Buy [0] -> Sell [1] -> observe toggle. Let's execute with waits."}
