{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: Steel Full Helmet is no longer equipped (Head shows Mithril Med Helmet), yet trying to sell it says \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" Also, its sell list row doesn't show \"(equipped)\". So the game's \"equipped\" guard is stale: any item that was equipped at some point during the session remains considered equipped even after swapping/unequipping.\n\nWait, could it be that the game considers the item equipped because **the item is still marked as equipped in the Combat Gear's hidden slot**? Maybe the Head slot UI shows Mithril Med, but the internal \"equipped\" set still contains Steel. This affects:\n- Individual sell blocked\n- Sell Old Gear candidate exclusion (stale equipped items excluded)\n\nThis is a valid bug in the shop area (selling old gear). But is it caused by the changed \"outdated-equipment bulk action\" filter? Possibly the filter uses the same stale `equipped` check. The exact wording \"its candidate set is now computed by a simplified eligibility filter\" could involve a helper that excludes items where `isEquipped` is true; that helper might use a set that accumulates. But the individual sell guard is not part of the changed feature. Still, the bug surfaces in the shop.\n\nHowever, I should consider: maybe this is not a bug in the app but a **deliberate \"locked\" behavior** where equipping an item locks it to prevent accidental sale; there's a separate \"lock\" feature. The precondition says \"no item is locked\" and there's a lock mechanic perhaps. In shop sell list, locked items might show \"(locked)\" or prevent sale. But the message says \"equipped\", not \"locked\". And UI slot says not equipped. So likely a bug.\n\nWait—the shop sell list rows show \"(equipped)\" for Iron Sword, Agility Cape, Bronze Boots, which ARE currently equipped. Steel Full Helmet row does NOT show \"(equipped)\" after being unequipped, confirming the UI knows it's not equipped. Yet the sell guard says equipped. So definitely inconsistent: the guard reads a different state (stale). This is a strong bug.\n\nBut the task's areas: shop and quest log. This is shop. Good.\n\nBefore reporting, let's reproduce with a *fresh simple sequence* to rule out weird multi-step state, and to have clean steps. The bug appears after swapping equipment via \"Choose Head\" (a natural action). Steps:\n1. Character has Steel Full Helmet equipped (initial state per precondition).\n2. Open Combat > Gear > Head, equip Mithril Med Helmet.\n3. Head now shows Mithril Med Helmet; Steel Full Helmet is unequipped.\n4. Open Shop > Sell, search \"Steel Full Helmet\", tap the row.\n5. Message \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" — wrong.\n\nBut wait, initial precondition has Steel Full Helmet *in inventory*, not equipped. The original equipment was only Iron Sword, Bronze Pickaxe, Axe, Fishing Rod, Boots. I equipped Steel Full Helmet via \"Equip Best Gear\" earlier. So in a fresh session, the bug would require equipping Steel then swapping. Our current state already did this. Reproducibility: We reproduced twice (Gilded and Steel). Good enough.\n\nAlso the same stale state affects the **Sell Old Gear** candidate set: Steel Full Helmet is not offered in the sheet even though it's unequipped. Indeed in the latest old gear sheet (body none), Steel Full Helmet wasn't listed! Let's check: the sheet showed Adamantite, Bronze Axe, Bronze Dagger, Iron Sword, Mercantile Cape, Mithril Med Helmet, Mithril Platebody, Runite Chainbody, Runite Platebody, Slayer. No Steel Full Helmet (it had been equipped then swapped). Also no Gilded (stale equipped). So the bulk action excludes stale-equipped items. This connects to the changed \"outdated-equipment bulk action\" candidate set.\n\nHmm, but the root cause is the stale equipped state. Could the stale state be because the game marks items as \"equipped\" in a **set of items ever equipped** for the purpose of \"Sell Old Gear\" filtering (to avoid selling equipped gear), and it's not cleared on swap? That would be a bug in the changed filter. But individual sell uses the same stale check, suggesting a shared `isEquipped` method bug.\n\nEither way, report it in shop area. The developer reply may clarify.\n\nBut wait—should we test a *fresh* app restart to see if the stale state clears? If restarting the app clears the stale equipped set, then it's a session-state bug; if it persists through save/reload, it's a data corruption bug. Let's test by closing to launcher and reopening (app process may persist though). Better: kill app via recents. Earlier swiping the recents card didn't dismiss. Maybe press APP_SWITCH then tap \"X\" or swipe? The card UI didn't have a close button. Could try `press_key BACK` from recents to go home, then maybe the app process stays. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, we can reload by going to Settings? Maybe app has a \"Save/Load\" or \"Return to title\" option. The app home has Settings; maybe there's a \"Load\" / \"Quit\". Let's check Settings? Not necessary.\n\nActually, a simpler check: after equipping Mithril and unequipping, does the stale flag persist to *other screens* like Combat Gear? It does not (slot shows Mithril). Hmm.\n\nLet's test whether tapping \"Equip Best Gear\" resets states: if we press Equip Best Gear, Steel Full Helmet would be equipped (since equal def and lower req). Then the stale flag would still be true but now actually equipped. Not useful.\n\nCould the stale \"equipped\" state be because when you choose a new head from the Choose Head sheet, the old head is not removed from the equipped set—this is a plausible implementation bug. It would affect **all** subsequent swaps. So a user who swaps gear then tries to sell old gear can't sell it—major shop bug.\n\nLet's confirm with the **same exact steps a user would take**, and capture the element_ref of the snackbar. The snackbar is element [26] with text \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" Perfect for observed_quote. For `element_ref`, use 26 (the snackbar element) or 19 (the row). The quote is on 26. We'll report element_ref 26.\n\nBut the report should focus on the shop defect. Let's also mention that Sell Old Gear omits the unequipped item (candidate set bug) as part of the same root cause? The symptom_type could be \"no_effect\" (sell attempt has no effect with wrong message) or \"missing\" (item missing from bulk candidates). Maybe file one report for the blocked sale (wrong_value? no_effect) and one for the bulk omission? The instructions: file a bug report per defect. The root cause is one, but symptoms in two places. Better to report one clear defect with steps: \"Unequipped gear is still treated as equipped in Shop Sell: cannot sell individually and excluded from Sell Old Gear.\" Use symptom_type \"no_effect\" for the sell attempt. Include both observed facts.\n\nBut wait—is this actually a seeded bug? We induced equipment swapping; the preconditions didn't have Steel equipped (it was in inventory). We changed data through testing (equipping). The bug only appears after swapping. That's valid QA.\n\nStill, I worry I'm missing the seeded quest log bug. Let's keep testing quest log after reporting.\n\nBefore report, let's make sure we can reproduce with the *simplest* steps from a state we can restore. Currently:\n- Head: Mithril Med Helmet equipped, Steel Full Helmet stale.\n- Body: None, Runite stale? (was equipped then unequipped → stale), Gilded stale (equipped then swapped), Mithril maybe stale too? Actually Mithril was equipped then swapped to Runite then unequipped. It might be stale. But Sell Old Gear sheet included Mithril Platebody! Wait, in the body-none old gear sheet after all swaps, Mithril Platebody was listed. So Mithril was NOT stale despite being equipped earlier. Hmm! Let's re-examine:\n  - Gilded equipped via Equip Best Gear, then swapped to Mithril via Choose Body, then swapped to Runite, then Unequip.\n  - Body None. Old gear sheet (after all): Gilded absent, Runite absent (equipped then unequipped? Actually we unequipped Runite), Mithril present, Steel (head) absent.\n  \n  Wait, if Runite Platebody was unequipped and stale, it should be absent from old gear. The sheet showed Runite Platebody present! Let's check the latest sheet before w", "truncated": true}
