{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed again. The snackbar is element [0] now. Use element_ref 0 and quote exact: \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\"\n\nBut wait: Is this maybe correct behavior because the **best gear** Steel is considered \"equipped\" in a loadout? The Head slot shows Mithril Med Helmet equipped. So no.\n\nLet's report this as a bug. Screen: \"Shop - Sell\". Element: \"Steel Full Helmet sell row\" / snackbar. Field: sell guard. Symptom type: no_effect (tapping row doesn't open sell sheet). Expected: item is unequipped (Head slot shows Mithril Med Helmet) so it should open the sell quantity sheet; observed message claims it's equipped.\n\nSteps: \n1. Open Combat > Gear > Head, equip Steel Full Helmet.\n2. Tap Head again and equip Mithril Med Helmet, replacing Steel Full Helmet.\n3. Confirm Head slot shows Mithril Med Helmet (Steel Full Helmet is no longer equipped).\n4. Open Shop > Sell, search \"Steel Full Helmet\", tap its row.\n5. Observe snackbar \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\"\n\nThis is a clean bug. Let's file it.\n\nShould we also mention that Sell Old Gear omits it? Could add to observed: \"it is also absent from Sell Old Gear\". But the report should be concise. Maybe mention expected includes both individual sell and bulk candidate. Could file a second report for the missing candidate in Sell Old Gear. The task says file a report per bug; maybe two reports for two symptoms of same root cause would be considered duplicate. Better one report focused on the individual sell guard, and maybe mention bulk. Hmm.\n\nActually, the changed area is \"Outdated-equipment bulk action: candidate set now computed by a simplified eligibility filter.\" The most relevant bug to that change is that Sell Old Gear excludes Steel Full Helmet (unequipped) incorrectly. The individual sell guard is a related symptom. I think report one bug titled \"Unequipped gear is still treated as equipped by the shop\" with both observations. Use element_ref 0 (snackbar). The developer will likely investigate the equipped-state bug.\n\nLet me file it now."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_RkZ4KkahPFKNVbBJUAbi3204", "tool": "mcp__device__file_report", "input": {"screen": "Shop > Sell", "element": "Steel Full Helmet sell row / Snackbar guard message", "field": "Sell action eligibility / equipped check", "symptom_type": "no_effect", "expected": "Steel Full Helmet is not equipped anymore (Combat > Gear > Head shows Mithril Med Helmet), so tapping its Sell row should open the sell-quantity sheet like any other unequipped item, and it should be eligible for the Sell Old Gear bulk action. The item should only be blocked/marked equipped while it is actually in the Head slot.", "observed": "Tapping the unequipped Steel Full Helmet row does nothing and shows \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\" The row itself does not display \"(equipped)\", yet the guard still treats it as equipped, and the item is also omitted from the Sell Old Gear candidate list.", "steps": ["Open Combat > Gear > Head and equip Steel Full Helmet.", "Tap the Head slot again and equip Mithril Med Helmet, replacing Steel Full Helmet.", "Confirm the Head slot now shows Mithril Med Helmet (Steel Full Helmet is unequipped).", "Open Shop > Sell, search \"Steel Full Helmet\" and tap its row.", "Observe the snackbar \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell.\""], "element_ref": 0, "observed_quote": "Steel Full Helmet is equipped. Unequip it first to sell."}}
