{"type": "thinking", "text": "Developer couldn't reproduce. Hmm. Maybe the bug requires the specific earlier state (Gilded/Equip Best Gear etc.). Or maybe the report steps were incomplete: when they equip Mithril Med Helmet while Steel is equipped, the game perhaps auto-unequips Steel properly in their build? But we observed it. Maybe the developer tried from a fresh save where Steel Full Helmet wasn't equipped first? Hmm.\n\nLet's think: maybe the guard is not based on \"equipped\" but on **locked** status; equipping items triggers a lock. Our earlier steps included \"Equip Best Gear\" which might have **locked** Steel Full Helmet (not equipped). The developer couldn't reproduce just by equipping/unequipping? Or maybe the guard depends on a different state.\n\nWait, when we equipped Steel Full Helmet the second time manually (via Choose Head), then replaced with Mithril Med, the bug still occurred. So the sequence should reproduce: equip Steel (it was already in inventory), then equip Mithril. Unless the \"equip\" action in our sequence didn't truly equip Steel because it was already considered \"equipped\" (stale)! Aha! Steel may have been stale-equipped all along from the earlier \"Equip Best Gear\" and never truly unequipped in the internal state; selecting Steel in Choose Head might have been a no-op / re-selected (since already considered equipped), and selecting Mithril changed the visible slot but left the internal set unchanged. So the steps as described may not reproduce on a fresh state because \"equip Steel\" may not work the same.\n\nLet's reconstruct from a cleaner state: We can't easily reset. But we can test the root scenario on a *never-equipped* item that is currently not equipped:\n- Body items: Mithril Platebody was equipped then swapped; it's currently included in old gear (not stale), so maybe fine.\n- Steel Full Helmet is stale from Equip Best Gear.\n- We need a fresh item never equipped in this session. Which items remain never equipped? Bronze Dagger (never equipped), Adamantite Platebody? Was never equipped individually (only \"Equip Best Gear\" chose Gilded; we manually equipped Mithril and Runite). Adamantite never equipped. Runite Chainbody never equipped. Slayer Platebody never equipped. Mercantile Cape never equipped. Mithril Med Helmet was equipped. \n- We can test the swap bug with a never-equipped item: equip **Adamantite Platebody** (never equipped), then equip **Runite Chainbody** (never equipped) to replace it, then try selling Adamantite. If the stale/equipped bug occurs, then it's reproducible on fresh items and my earlier steps should work with different items. If it doesn't occur, then the bug is about the items that were part of \"Equip Best Gear\" (Steel/Gilded) being permanently locked.\n\nLet's test that. Equip Adamantite, then Runite Chainbody, then sell Adamantite. Body is currently None. Head Mithril Med. Let's do:\nCombat→Gear→Body→Adamantite→ then Body→Runite Chain→ then Shop Sell search Adamantite→tap.\n\nIf Adamantite is blocked, the bug is general; if not, the issue is \"Equip Best Gear\" or specific items remaining flagged.\n\nLet's test. The shop sell screen is current; tap Combat bottom (320,2169)? Actually it's a snackbar open; tap still works. Let's go Combat and wait."}
