{"type": "thinking", "text": "Still dead.\n\nLet me consider whether the broken pipe is caused by too many operations/session length, and whether a new session/device would be needed. I cannot spawn.\n\nMaybe I should keep retrying every so often. Meanwhile, let me reflect on the developer's rejection: \"could not reproduce with the steps given.\" Perhaps because my steps assumed Steel Full Helmet was equipped initially, which in a fresh build it's not. They might have tried without the prior weird state. But we did carefully re-equip Steel then swap Mithril and reproduce. Yet maybe in their reproduction, equipping Steel while it's already \"stale equipped\" was a no-op, so the state didn't match. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the actual bug is easier to reproduce from the initial state:\n- Initial: Head=None, Body=None, Cape=None, but inventory has Steel Full Helmet, Mithril Med Helmet, Gilded, etc.\n- Press **\"Equip Best Gear\"** (Combat Gear). This equips Steel Full Helmet, Gilded Platebody, Agility Cape.\n- Now swap Head to Mithril Med Helmet (or Body to Mithril). Then try selling the replaced item.\nWe did that and reproduced. The developer may not have tried \"Equip Best Gear\" first. The message \"Steel Full Helmet is equipped\" persisted because the old item from Equip Best Gear wasn't properly unequipped when swapping. If you manually equip Steel (not via Equip Best Gear), maybe the app doesn't add it to the stale set and swapping works fine—so the bug is specifically in **Equip Best Gear's equipment bookkeeping**. The steps should emphasize starting from \"Equip Best Gear\".\n\nLet's reconstruct the actual first occurrence:\n- Initial precondition: no head/body/cape equipped.\n- We tapped \"Equip Best Gear\", which equipped Steel Full Helmet (Head), Gilded Platebody (Body), Agility Cape.\n- Later we chose Mithril Platebody for Body → Gilded became stale-equipped.\n- Later chose Mithril Med Helmet for Head → Steel became stale-equipped.\nSo the bug likely: **\"Equip Best Gear\" marks items equipped in a way that swapping them later doesn't clear their equipped status** (or it equips them into slots without registering them for removal). The individual sell guard then thinks they're still equipped.\n\nTo reproduce cleanly:\n1. Start with no head/body/cape equipped (precondition).\n2. Press \"Equip Best Gear\" → Head=Steel Full Helmet, Body=Gilded Platebody, Cape=Agility Cape.\n3. Change Head to Mithril Med Helmet (or Body to Mithril Platebody).\n4. Try selling the previously auto-equipped item → blocked with \"is equipped.\"\nThis likely reproduces. The developer may have missed step 2.\n\nOur report's steps should include Equip Best Gear first. Let's update the report when the device returns. We can't file now. We'll retry.\n\nLet me also note: The bug may be in \"Equip Best Gear\" (not in the changed list) but manifests in shop. Task areas include shop; okay.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the actual seeded bug is the **bulk \"Sell Old Gear\" filter** being based on \"equipped set\" that doesn't update after Equip Best Gear swaps, causing items to be excluded. The dev might expect.\n\nLet's wait for device recovery. Try observe again."}
